        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നീ (nī, familiar \"you\") from Proto-Dravidian nīn — the same native root as Tamil nī, Kannada nīnu, Telugu nuvvu. നിങ്ങൾ (niṅṅaḷ) is the respectful/plural \"you\" — nī + a plural ending, the exact cousin of Tamil nīṅgaḷ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: respect by the plural",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nī (familiar) vs. niṅṅaḷ (respectful, literally plural) — the family's shared politeness-by-plural, same idea as French vous. For a first meeting, niṅṅaḷ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
